the need to assess accuracy","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"a74235bc-c2c0-532b-8628-c47542450abe","text":"It enables rapid distribution across organizational and geographic boundaries","isCorrect":true,"position":1},{"id":"58d42bfa-1e99-591e-976d-8481c2bd8ee5","text":"It confines information to one filing cabinet","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"76d4d75a-1a4a-5ace-82f2-09d83adde2cf","text":"It prevents international communication","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"c543b843-ca46-589c-baed-b057b7767e1f","position":116,"prompt":"Why is secure disposal an information-processing step?","explanation":"Retention should end with controlled deletion or destruction appropriate to the sensitivity of the information.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Information Processing and Society","fingerprint":"ff61bea0cb3bf39ca03042231aaa141e25787439335c2aaefe3cb8c55ee92857","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"COS 101 lecture note, Module Five","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFile":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_cos101_200_v1","sourceReference":"COS 101 lecture note, Module Five","technicalAccuracyReviewCompleted":true,"humanVerificationRequired":true},"options":[{"id":"f6979124-3c9e-565a-8a8c-740ebba8b2f4","text":"Information no longer needed may still create privacy or security risk","isCorrect":true,"position":0},{"id":"2cbda40d-b44e-5434-b408-276694c4af7f","text":"Deleted data always remain fully public","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"1d663ba5-a541-56c4-b58d-c4e0b758b79d","text":"Disposal increases storage capacity without removing anything","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"48b85085-bbce-5404-a786-36b32fca77f7","text":"Only paper records require protection","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"419f3daf-bbaa-55e5-8514-c2199cba0ffc","position":117,"prompt":"A form accepts an examination score of 145 percent. Which control should have prevented the error first?","explanation":